        <profileDesc>
            <creation/>
            <abstract>
                <p>Magic prayer against the demon Tǝgrǝtyā, who is called ‘Dǝgrǝtyā’ in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/EMIP02043#ms_i6">Washington, D.C., Howard University School of Divinity, Tweed Codex 094: Malkǝʾ-hymn to the guardian angel (in ms_i6)</ref>.
                    According to <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/H8WBU22B"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Strelcyn1972Wellcome"/><title level="a">Catalogue of Ethiopian Manuscripts of the Wellcome Institute of the History of Medicine in London</title><title level="j">Bulletin of the School of Oriental and African Studies, University of London</title><author><forename>Stefan</forename><surname>Strelcyn</surname></author><date>1972</date><biblScope unit="volume">35</biblScope><biblScope unit="issue">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">27-55</biblScope><note type="url">http://www.jstor.org/stable/612793</note><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1972Wellcome</note></note><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1972Wellcome</note><citedRange unit="page">52</citedRange></bibl> 
                    following <bibl><ptr target="bm:Guidi1935Vocabolario2nd"/><citedRange unit="page">327</citedRange></bibl>,
                    ‘Tǝgrǝtyā’ (also: ‘Tǝgridā’) is a demon or ‘devil who stays in lonely places and causes epilepsy’. The verbal plural forms in 
                    <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/EMIP02043#ms_i6">Washington, D.C., Howard University School of Divinity, Tweed Codex 094: Malkǝʾ-hymn to the guardian angel (in ms_i6)</ref> and <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr66#ms_i4">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 66: Prayer against Tǝgrǝtyā (in ms_i4)</ref> are possibly 
                    grammatically incongruent forms which evolved because of the omission of entities, which have been named before or through
                    the common use in magic prayers, which are normally directed against various demonic entities.</p>
            </abstract>
